Here’s what’s in `/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue`.

## 1. Exact element (copy in file: **「只顯示今日有課老師」** — no **「的」** before **「老師」**)

The string lives inside a **`<label>`** that wraps a checkbox and a **`<span>`** for the text.

```81:88:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
                <label
                  v-if="!isWeekOverview && !isTeacher"
                  class="filter-toggle toolbar-hide-empty-toggle"
                  title="開啟後只顯示今日有排課的老師欄；此模式下無法點空格快速排課"
                >
                  <input type="checkbox" v-model="hideEmptyTeacherColumns" />
                  <span>只顯示今日有課老師</span>
                </label>
```

- **Structure**: `label.filter-toggle.toolbar-hide-empty-toggle` → `input[type="checkbox"]` + `span` (label text).
- **`filter-toggle`**: used only as a class name here; there is **no** `.filter-toggle` rule in this file (and no other `.filter-toggle` styles in `frontend/` besides unrelated `filter-toggles` in `StudentsList.vue`). Styling comes from **`.toolbar-filters .toolbar-hide-empty-toggle`**.

Related copy (empty state hint) at **lines 177–179** mentions the same wording with inline styles on a `<div>` (not the toggle itself).

---

## 2. CSS for that control

Toggle-specific rules:

```4124:4148:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
.toolbar-filters .toolbar-hide-empty-toggle {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 6px;
  padding: 8px 10px;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e2e8f0);
  border-radius: 8px;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.2;
  background: #fff;
  color: var(--text, #334155);
  cursor: pointer;
  user-select: none;
  white-space: nowrap;
  height: 38px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
  flex-shrink: 0;
}
.toolbar-filters .toolbar-hide-empty-toggle:hover {
  border-color: var(--primary, #2563eb);
}
.toolbar-filters .toolbar-hide-empty-toggle input[type="checkbox"] {
  accent-color: var(--primary, #2563eb);
  margin: 0;
}
```

Parent row for all filters (room select, search inputs, optional leave button, this label):

```4081:4088:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
.toolbar-filters {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 8px;
  align-items: center;
  min-width: 0;
  width: 100%;
}
```

---

## 3. Wrappers: fixed width / overflow (tablet-relevant)

Ancestor chain in the template:

- **Lines 13–124**: `.smart-cal-toolbar`
- **Lines 51–123**: `.toolbar-row.toolbar-row-secondary`
- **Lines 64–122**: `.toolbar-secondary-line.toolbar-secondary-line--filters`
- **Lines 65–117**: `.toolbar-secondary-mid`
- **Lines 66–89**: `.toolbar-filters` ← direct parent of the `<label>`

Toolbar / filter line constraints:

```3496:3558:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
.smart-cal-toolbar {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: stretch;
  gap: 0;
  padding: 12px 16px;
  background: #fff;
  border: 1px solid var(--border-color, #e2e8f0);
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  min-width: 0;
  max-width: 100%;
  overflow-x: hidden;
}
...
.toolbar-secondary-line--filters {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
  gap: 10px 12px;
  align-items: start;
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
}
.toolbar-secondary-mid {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: stretch;
  gap: 10px;
  min-width: 0;
  max-width: 100%;
}
```

**Takeaways**

- **No fixed pixel width** on the label or these wrappers; layout uses **`max-width: 100%`**, **`min-width: 0`**, and a **grid** for the filters row (`minmax(0, 1fr) auto`).
- **`.smart-cal-toolbar`** sets **`overflow-x: hidden`** (line 3508), which can clip horizontal overflow if something extends past the bar without wrapping.
- The toggle uses **`white-space: nowrap`** and **`flex-shrink: 0`**, so the label does not shrink or wrap; it moves to the next flex row when **`.toolbar-filters`** wraps (`flex-wrap: wrap`).

Outer page header wrapper:

```3450:3454:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
.smart-cal-top {
  margin-bottom: 24px;
  max-width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
}
```

---

## 4. Filter toolbar area + tablet breakpoints that touch it

**Filter toolbar block**: **`div.smart-cal-toolbar`** (line 13), secondary row **`toolbar-row-secondary`** (51), filters line **`toolbar-secondary-line--filters`** (64), filters **`toolbar-filters`** (66).

**Media queries in this file that affect that toolbar / filters row** (not the teacher grid):

| Breakpoint | Lines | Effect on this area |
|------------|-------|---------------------|
| **`max-width: 600px`** | 4602–4611 | **`.toolbar-secondary-line--filters`**: `grid-template-columns: 1fr` — stacks the mid column and action buttons vertically. **`.toolbar-secondary-actions`**: full width, can wrap. |
| **`max-width: 768px`** | 4615+ | **`.smart-cal-header`** column layout, **`.week-nav`** wrap, day tabs smaller — **no rule** named for `.toolbar-hide-empty-toggle` or `.toolbar-filters` here. |
| **`max-width: 640px`** | 4670–4688 | **`.toolbar-filters { width: 100%; }`**; **`.filter-select, .filter-input`** get `flex: 1; min-width: 0` — the **checkbox label is not** in that selector list, so it keeps its own flex behavior (`flex-shrink: 0`, nowrap). |

**`max-width: 900px` and `1100px`** blocks (4571–4600) mostly target **`.teacher-grid` / columns**, not this toolbar.

